<title>SRI LANKA: CRICKET-RAIN HALTS INDIA V PAKISTAN MATCH.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-RAIN HALTS INDIA V PAKISTAN MATCH.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rain and poor light halted the Asia Cup match between India and Pakistan at Colombo's Singhalese Sports Club ground on Sunday.</p>
<p>Pakistan were 19 for 3 in five overs when players left the field.</p>
<p>Cricket officials said they expected the match to resume shortly after rain stopped. They said if the two teams were unable to play at least 25 overs each, the match would be replayed on Monday.</p>
</text>
